{"_id":"68a736208ec3d8323af189b7","nodeId":"w0i5Dxp40XS2HnF5nXeZI","roadmapSlug":"ios","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:12.170Z","description":"# Basics / Creating Animations\n\nCreating animations with Core Animation involves working with CALayer and CAAnimation subclasses. CABasicAnimation animates a single property from one value to another, while CAKeyframeAnimation defines multiple values along an animation path. Animations are applied to layer properties like position, opacity, transform, and background color.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"CALayer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/quartzcore/calayer","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf85cb"},{"type":"official","title":"CAKeyframeAnimation Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/quartzcore/cakeyframeanimation","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf85cc"},{"type":"article","title":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/quartzcore/cabasicanimation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/quartzcore/cabasicanimation","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf85cd"},{"type":"article","title":"What is CALayer?","url":"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/example-code/calayer/what-is-calayer","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf85ce"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:24.838Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ios/content/w0i5Dxp40XS2HnF5nXeZI.md"}